    skos:definition "A recurring governed invocation. Rather than owning its own cron/timezone/invokes fields, a Practice references a ProcessSpec (execution.yaml) whose START step is kind: TIMER -- the schedule lives once, on the process, not twice (once here and once conceptually on whatever the source schema's separate WorkflowDeclaration would have needed). This removes the source schema's `schedule` and `invokes` blocks entirely; `delivery`, `autonomy`, `budgetRef`, and `enabled` are unchanged." ;
