    skos:definition "A Realm is a governance, privacy and security boundary. Spheres group work inside a Realm without being security boundaries (canonical decision 12). `ingress` is the same shape one level up, for DNS instead of workspace grouping: `RealmIngressBinding` carries no audience, policy, capability or other authority-bearing attribute, so a subdomain stays routing only by construction, never a security boundary -- `enforcement` on this same spec remains the only field that is." ;
